      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is the situation of this API on the SDK side:\n\n- class Image has a hidden getTransform: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/media/java/android/media/Image.java;l\u003d232?q\u003dcase:yes%20getTransform\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain:frameworks%2Fbase%2Fmedia%2Fjava%2F\nWhen I talked to John in February he said he believes this was a miss (since the API exists in SurfaceTexture)\n\n- SurfaceImage that extends Image implements this here: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/media/java/android/media/ImageReader.java;l\u003d1252?q\u003dcase:yes%20getTransform\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain:frameworks%2Fbase%2Fmedia%2Fjava%2F\n\n- WriterSurfaceImage implements it here:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/media/java/android/media/ImageWriter.java;l\u003d1112?q\u003dcase:yes%20getTransform\u0026ss\u003dandroid%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain:frameworks%2Fbase%2Fmedia%2Fjava%2F\n\nI chose to go with AImage::getTransformMatrix() to match the existing SurfaceTexture::getTransformMatrix(), but if you think we should go with AImage::getTransform() to match Image::getTransform(), let me know. I\u0027m not very familiar with the Java side, but I believe I can put a CL together for that part too. Since the documentation mentions mTransform is set during nativeImageSetup():\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/base/media/java/android/media/ImageReader.java;l\u003d1425\nI believe this should be a simple change (basically moving the implementation up to the Image and making the API public),",
      "parentUuid": "6abbce5a_4d3a6c12",
      "revId": "fd4aed846eb9348783fde28b940f9af803641446",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
